# ─── Optional scientific libraries (Category C) — LAZY LOADED ───
# IMPORTANT FOR SPEED: These heavy libraries (cobra, rdkit, biopython, pandas,
# statsmodels, sbol2, ...) used to import at startup, adding 25-45 seconds on
# older machines. Now each one loads ONLY when first needed, via _ensure_*()
# helpers below. The HAS_* flags start as None ("not yet checked") and become
# True/False after the first check. Startup is now near-instant; the small
# one-time load happens when you first open the section that needs the library.
#
# The module-level names (cobra, Chem, pd, sm, ...) start as None and get
# filled in by the _ensure_*() functions. Code that uses them should call the
# matching _ensure_*() first (or check the HAS_* flag, which triggers loading).

